00:23:57.340 --> 00:24:16.880
<v Julia Dewitt>The cave is almost 1,000 feet deep and two and a half football fields wide. The main thing that lives in the pitch darkness is a species of strange little blind white cave shrimp. Otherwise, the cave is dark, deep, and dead.
<v Julia Dewitt>洞穴深近1000英尺，宽达两个半橄榄球场。生活在漆黑环境中的主要生物是一种奇特的盲白色洞穴虾。除此之外，洞穴深暗、广袤且死寂。

00:24:16.880 --> 00:24:31.150
<v Julia Dewitt>This cave is a dangerous place for humans. And it's basically totally inaccessible to almost all of us. But for deep water divers, this is heaven.
<v Julia Dewitt>这个洞穴对人类来说是个危险的地方。基本上，我们大多数人都无法进入。但对于深潜潜水员来说，这是天堂。

00:24:31.150 --> 00:24:42.490
<v Julia Dewitt>There are only a very few divers on the planet that have ever been anywhere near the bottom of this cave. And only about a dozen recreational divers ever dive to these kinds of depths, period.
<v Julia Dewitt>世界上只有极少数潜水员曾接近过这个洞穴的底部。且总共只有十几名休闲潜水员曾潜入这种深度。

00:24:42.490 --> 00:25:00.670
<v Julia Dewitt>Don is one of these extreme divers. He met another of these deep water divers, a guy named Dave Shaw, back in 2002. They were immediately friends, and a couple of years later, Don took Dave to dive Bushman's.
<v Julia Dewitt>Don是这些极限潜水员之一。他在2002年认识了另一位深潜潜水员，名叫Dave Shaw。他们立刻成了朋友，几年后，Don带Dave去潜布什曼洞穴。

00:25:00.670 --> 00:25:09.100
<v Julia Dewitt>On dive day, they got to the puddle and Dave went in first. Dave swam down through the slot, and the cave opened up below him.
<v Julia Dewitt>潜水当天，他们到了水坑，Dave先下去。Dave游过裂缝，下方的洞穴豁然开朗。

00:25:09.100 --> 00:25:20.450
<v Julia Dewitt>While he was going down, he was doing something called laying a shot line. Basically, he was leaving a trail of rope in the total darkness. This is the only way he knew how to get out of the cave.
<v Julia Dewitt>当他下潜时，他在执行一项任务，叫做布设引导绳。基本上，他是在漆黑一片中留下一条绳索路径。这是他知道离开洞穴的唯一方法。

00:25:20.450 --> 00:25:30.180
<v Don Shirley>You're in pitch black, absolute pitch black. So if you shine a light in any direction, it will disappear. The darkness will eat the light.
<v Don Shirley>你身处绝对的漆黑中，伸手不见五指。所以如果你向任何方向打光，它都会消失。黑暗会吞噬光线。

00:25:30.180 --> 00:25:41.590
<v Don Shirley>Basically, being 900 foot in a cave, you might as well be on the moon. In fact, I think more people have walked on the moon than have actually been to those sort of depths in caves.
<v Don Shirley>基本上，身处洞穴900英尺深处，你就像在月球上一样。事实上，我认为去过月球的人比曾到达这种深度的洞穴潜水员还要多。

00:25:41.590 --> 00:25:49.880
<v Julia Dewitt>This sounds unbelievable, but it's true. More people have been on the moon than have been to the depths that these guys have.
<v Julia Dewitt>这听起来不可思议，但却是事实。去过月球的人比曾到达这些家伙探索深度的人还要多。

00:25:49.880 --> 00:26:00.880
<v Julia Dewitt>Now Dave was exploring on the bare floor of the cavern. There's nothing to see but his light in the black and the white rope that he dragged with him. Then suddenly--
